KZ3 patch 2080 (RSX pass 75): the clean-bitmap skip is exact by default, a writer diagnostic for location 0, and
NV3089 blit time/bytes plus an opt-in row copy. the RE notes "Pass 75".
1. LD_TEX_CLEAN (2079) now applies to location 1 only by default (r74-chk: 0 misses there in ~5,100 frames); location 0
   keeps the 2046 rule (6 "bitmap clean, hash differs" DXT1 misses at 0:0x0FFxxxxx in r74-chk). LD_TEX_CLEAN=2 = both
   locations (round-74 behaviour), 0 = off. LD_TEX_HASH_CHECK=1 still checks location 0 under the default.
2. LD_TEX_WRITER=1 (off by default): per 64 KB page of location 0, the tracked path and frame of the last note (SPU put,
   host file read, NV0039, NV3089, NV308A, surface write-back, explicit EA note; per-thread tag). Each location-0
   [tex-clean-miss] prints [tex-clean-writer] (last hash frame, newest tracked write, per-page writers): "untracked
   writer" = nothing noted since the last hash. LD_TEX_WATCH=1 (with it) write-protects the missed span once and logs the
   first store into each 4 KB page ([tex-watch] host rip / [rsp] as exe offsets, thread id, guest offset).
3. [perf-nv3089] per RSX_PERF period (walker window): blits, whole-method ms, GPU mirror/resolve ms, guest copy ms,
   row-copied blits, MB written; tools/smoke/walk_budget.py reports them. LD_NV3089_ROWS=1 (default off): unscaled
   blits copy each clipped row with one memcpy (libs/video/rsx_nv3089_rows.h; same idea as upstream PR 334) and keep the
   destination page note; it falls back to the per-pixel loop on source/destination overlap, a 4 GB wrap, or a store
   hook in the destination (write watch, SPU line reservation, PPU reservation store). Host test
   tools/smoke/test_nv3089_rows.sh (byte-identical to the per-pixel loop over 20,000 random blits).
Refreshed for v0.15.0 (SPU pass 85): upstream's draw-engine calls nv3089_engine_read/_wrote sit next to the copy;
the guest-copy timer starts after nv3089_engine_read, the engine write-back still runs for both copy paths.
